{
  "about": [
    "The Zen View's contents, written as data: the grid's cards in order, and each strip's rows.",
    "",
    "Both evaluators replay it. `src-tauri/tests/operations/zen_contents_conformance.rs` runs every",
    "case through `crate::filters::zen`; `src/utils/zen-contents-conformance.test.ts` runs the same",
    "cases through `zen-contents.ts`. Neither side generates this file.",
    "",
    "A board's nodes are written as in `preset-filters.json`. `filter` is the tab's shared filter —",
    "`preset`, `showOnAgent`, `showReview`, `startHidesCheckedWaits` and `privateMode`, each",
    "defaulting as the app's does — which the Zen View reads under its own presets. `options` is what the tab asks of the",
    "view: the two strips, the Agentic pill, and the two app-wide grid settings. The focus exemption",
    "is a render-time overlay on the view's selection and is not here.",
    "",
    "`views` says which views read the board under a preset of their own: `locked` is that",
    "preset, or null for a view that reads the tab's own.",
    "",
    "A node may carry `derivedInProgress`: a Task that reads In Progress (Doing) only from its sub-items, not from a status held by hand — a Compound Task, or a parent raised to it. The grid drops such a card while an In Progress item beneath it is drawn too, and keeps it when that item is not drawn."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "the grid is do in board order with review first, whatever the tab's own preset",
      "spec": "zen-view.md — The grid is the List View's Task rows under Do, Review cards first, less every delegated Task.",
      "board": "zen",
      "filter": {
        "preset": "plan",
        "showReview": true
      },
      "options": {
        "commitments": true,
        "expectations": true
      },
      "expect": {
        "tasks": [
          "task-review",
          "task-progress",
          "task-sub",
          "task-doing"
        ],
        "commitments": [
          "commitment-open"
        ],
        "expectations": [
          "expectation-delegated",
          "expectation-person",
          "expectation-checked"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a started task joins the grid while the zen view's own setting says so",
      "spec": "zen-view.md — Whether a Started Task counts is the Zen View's own setting, not the Do preset's.",
      "board": "zen",
      "filter": {
        "preset": "plan",
        "showReview": true
      },
      "options": {
        "commitments": true,
        "expectations": true,
        "showsStarted": true
      },
      "expect": {
        "tasks": [
          "task-review",
          "task-progress",
          "task-started",
          "task-sub",
          "task-doing"
        ],
        "commitments": [
          "commitment-open"
        ],
        "expectations": [
          "expectation-delegated",
          "expectation-person",
          "expectation-checked"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a compound task's card is drawn only while its setting is on, and its sub-items always",
      "spec": "zen-view.md — Off, a Compound Task's card is not drawn; its sub-items still are, by their own status.",
      "board": "zen",
      "filter": {
        "preset": "plan",
        "showReview": true
      },
      "options": {
        "commitments": true,
        "expectations": true,
